Upstream fix https://github.com/recastnavigation/recastnavigation/pull/796
(9f4ce64): buildPolyDetail indexes tris[0] while sampling the detail mesh, and
on a polygon whose triangulation came out empty that is an out-of-bounds read
that asserts in debug and crashes in release on large-scale generation.

diff --git a/Recast/Source/RecastMeshDetail.cpp b/Recast/Source/RecastMeshDetail.cpp
--- a/Recast/Source/RecastMeshDetail.cpp
+++ b/Recast/Source/RecastMeshDetail.cpp
@@ -878,6 +878,7 @@ static bool buildPolyDetail(rcContext* ctx, const float* in, const int nin,
 				pt[0] = s[0]*sampleDist + getJitterX(i)*cs*0.1f;
 				pt[1] = s[1]*chf.ch;
 				pt[2] = s[2]*sampleDist + getJitterY(i)*cs*0.1f;
+				if (tris.size() == 0) continue;
 				float d = distToTriMesh(pt, verts, nverts, &tris[0], tris.size()/4);
 				if (d < 0) continue; // did not hit the mesh.
 				if (d > bestd)
